      "date": "1906",
      "kind": "construction",
      "description": "Recorded in the city's survey of the Van Ness Avenue automobile corridor as built for use as a retail; auto repair and sales 1. Built as a temporary clothing store for Roos Brothers while downtown was rebuilt after the earthquake and fire. It is the only one of Van Ness Avenue's temporary post-fire commercial buildings still standing.",
